{"level":"info","message":"Generated Response:","responseText":"Okay, I understand. It sounds like you're carrying a lot right now, and feeling overwhelmed is a really tough place to be. It's completely understandable that you're feeling this way.\n\nLet's try to unpack this a bit. To help me understand what's contributing to this feeling, could you tell me more about what's been happening lately? What areas of your life feel the most overwhelming right now – is it work, relationships, something else?\n\nIn the meantime, let's try a quick grounding exercise. Sometimes when we feel overwhelmed, our thoughts race and we lose touch with the present. Let's take a few deep breaths together. Inhale deeply through your nose, hold it for a few seconds, and exhale slowly through your mouth. Do this a few times.\n\nNow, try the 5-4-3-2-1 technique. Acknowledge FIVE things you can *see* around you. Then acknowledge FOUR things you can *physically feel* (e.g., the texture of your clothes, the chair you're sitting on). Then acknowledge THREE things you can *hear*. Then TWO things you can *smell*. Finally, ONE thing you can *taste*. This exercise can help bring you back to the present moment and reduce the feeling of being overwhelmed.\n\nRemember, you're not alone in feeling this way, and we can work through this together. Sharing more details will help us identify specific triggers and develop strategies to manage these feelings more effectively. We can explore things like time management, prioritization, and even relaxation techniques in more detail.\n\nAnd please remember, if at any point you feel like you're in crisis, please reach out to a crisis hotline or mental health professional immediately. I'm here to support you, but I'm not a substitute for emergency services. How does that sound?","timestamp":"2025-08-10T16:15:43.022Z"}
